course: dictionary
lesson: 14571
title: A word from the forest floor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pinecone is a word you may meet in stories, science and nature books. The words around it give you clues. «Mia picked up a brown pinecone from under the pine tree.» Picked up, brown and under a pine tree tell you it is something small you can hold, found on the ground.
explain: «The pinecone's scales opened wide on the hot, dry day.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A hard, woody case on a pine tree fits, because the scales open to let the seeds out in dry weather.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Lucy filled a pinecone with seeds for the birds.» Put in the meaning: Lucy filled a hard, woody case from a pine tree with seeds for the birds. It still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A pinecone is the hard, woody, scaly case on a pine tree.
fact: A pinecone holds a pine tree's seeds and keeps them safe.
fact: In dry weather, a pinecone's scales open and the seeds can fall out.
fact: In damp weather, a pinecone's scales close up tight.
fact: People use pinecones to forecast the weather, and in crafts they can be made into bird feeders.
exercise: «Mia picked up a brown pinecone from under the pine tree.» What is a pinecone? | A kind of pine tree | *A hard, woody, scaly case on a pine tree that holds seeds | A soft, juicy fruit that grows on a bush | A small brown bird that lives in trees
exercise: When the weather is damp, what do a pinecone's scales do? | Turn green and grow leaves | Open wide to let the seeds fall out | *Close up tight | Fall off the tree
exercise: Which words in «Lucy filled a pinecone with seeds for the birds» tell you what a pinecone can hold? | birds | for | garden | *seeds
test: «In dry weather the pinecone opened and let its seeds fall to the ground.» What does opened show? | The pinecone grew into a new tree | The tree lost all its leaves | The pinecone turned into a bird | *The scales spread out so the seeds can escape
test: Which is a fact about pinecones? | They can sing in the morning | *They hold a pine tree's seeds and keep them safe | They are soft and juicy to eat | They only grow in deserts
exam: Ella says a pinecone is a soft, juicy fruit. What is the correct meaning? | A soft, juicy fruit | *A hard, woody, scaly case on a pine tree | A kind of cloud | A type of bird
